Z||000000||GT Bastard||04-23-2000||06:53 PM||||At the wiring harness junction block in front of the battery, I noticed that it looks melted...  Actually, I noticed this awhile back.  None of the wires look charred, but the plastic that the wiring goes into seems to be melted into the wiring.  How easy it is to change out the whole harness?  Thanks fellas...<P>ps-- The car still runs fine||||reg||11
Z||000001||80's BOY||04-23-2000||08:38 PM||||this problem just cost me $167 towing from some street races last month. seems to be a bad call on GM's design dept. i went to meet a guy with a cavalier that bet me 50 bucks he could take me on the street on the local 1/4 mile. while we were all sitting there talking smack, my car falls dead. no lights,engine,interior, nothing. severe embarassment. it had to be towed before i got busted. fixed it in 20 minutes the next morning. my suggestion: take out the rinky-dink power cable distribution block, and get a heavy duty block and put larger connectors on your power wires. i used a block that is made for wiring amplifiers for heavy duty stereo systems. better safe than sorry. for a quick fix, pull off the wires and clean the connections and the small metal strip between the two poles. this is why your wires are melting. someday, somewhere, you will get left stranded because of this. trust me, you need to fix it QUICKLY. it might save you some $$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$||||reg||6
